    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32284" root="غلق" body-key="g">
    
      7 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انغلق</span></b> ; (MA, TA;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَلِقَ</span></b> , (TA,) inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَلَقٌ</span>; (KL;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استغلق</span></b> ; (KL, TA;) said
of a door, (MA, KL, TA,) <i>It was,</i> or <i>became,
locked,</i> or <i>bolted;</i> or <i>closed,</i> or <i>shut;</i> (MA, KL;)
or <i>difficult to be opened:</i> (TA:) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انغلق</span> is the
<i>contr. of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انفتح</span>. (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See a verse cited voce
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوِيْئَةٌ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روأ</span>. [And see also 10.]

